<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Varano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century–<a href="/years/1539">1539</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Da Varano family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Varano were a noble family who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camerino">Camerino</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> from the second half of the 13th century until 1539. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentile-da-varano">Gentile da Varano</a> led the city from 1262, and his descendants served as papal vicars and condottieri. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a> had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-cesare-da-varano">Giulio Cesare da Varano</a> and his sons killed in 1502, but the family returned, became dukes in 1515 and lost Camerino to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Pope Paul III</a>.</p></div>
